SOURCE="Philippine Statistics Authority";
NOTEX="<strong>Indicator:</strong> Gross Domestic Product (in thousand PhP)##<strong>Definition:</strong>##Gross Domestic Product (GDP) measures the production of all resident producers. It is the monetary value of all final goods and services produced within a"
"n economy at a given time.##See more: <a href = 'https://psa.gov.ph/system/files/eiad/Quarterly-and-Annual-Gross-Domestic-Product-Sources-and-Methods.pdf'>https://psa.gov.ph/system/files/eiad/Quarterly-and-Annual-Gross-Domestic-Product-Sources-and-Method"
"s.pdf</a>##<strong>Method of Computation:</strong>##The GDP at the provincial and highly urbanized city (HUC) level is computed using production approach. GDP is derived by adding the gross value added (GVA) of all resident producer units, plus the value"
" of taxes less subsidies on products. GVA is the value of gross output less the value of intermediate consumption.##<strong>Source of Basic Data:</strong>##Data are sourced from both survey and administrative sources. Major sources for the benchmark esti"
"mates include Census of Philippine Business Industry (CPBI), Updated list of establishments (ULE), Family Income and Expenditure Survey (FIES), while surveys and administrative data from various stakeholders were utilized in non-benchmark compilation.##<"
"strong>Note/s:</strong>##i. Provincial Product Accounting (PPA) is an accounting framework, which is aligned with the Philippine System of National Accounts (PSNA), that aims to present a comprehensive picture of the provincial and Highly Urbanized City "
"(HUC) economies.#ii. Figures for the City of Makati exclude the Embo Barangays starting in 2022, following their transfer to the City of Taguig.";
NEXT-UPDATE="20270828 10:00";
PX-SERVER="OpenSTAT";
SURVEY="Provincial Product Accounts";
UPDATE-FREQUENCY="Annually";
